1. DashCast (https://github.com/stestagg/dashcast): DashCast is a custom receiver application that allows users to cast arbitrary web pages to a Chromecast device. Use Case: Dashboard displays, digital signage, showing web-based metrics on a TV.
2. Shaka Player Demo (https://github.com/shaka-project/shaka-player/tree/main/demo): A robust demonstration app for Google's Shaka Player. Use Case: DRM-protected video playback testing, adaptive bitrate (DASH/HLS) streaming debugging, and advanced media capabilities.
3. CastHelloText-chrome (https://github.com/googlecast/CastHelloText-chrome): A simple reference application from Google. Use Case: Learning how to send basic text messages and commands from a Chrome browser sender to a custom receiver, ideal for diagnostics and basic IPC testing.
4. Cast-Player-Sample (https://github.com/googlecast/Cast-Player-Sample): Google's advanced media player sample. Use Case: Creating customized video players, styling the receiver UI, handling queues, and working with the Media Player Library (MPL).
5. Catt (Cast All The Things) (https://github.com/skorokithakis/catt): While primarily a sender CLI, it interfaces with default/custom receivers. Use Case: Command-line diagnostics, casting local files, YouTube videos, and arbitrary URLs to a Chromecast for testing.
6. Chromecast-Kiosk (Various implementations): Custom web receivers designed to cycle through URLs. Use Case: Office kiosks, home assistant dashboards (like Home Assistant Cast), and automated visual reporting.
